window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-031.json",{"day":31,"title":"The Forest Station Before the Fire","targetWords":[{"word":"incur","gloss":"承担","context":"Rangers must incur maintenance costs rather than postpone every repair.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"kiss","gloss":"亲吻","context":"A child offered her grandmother a kiss; another began to blush when praised for reporting smoke promptly.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"outbreak","gloss":"爆发","context":"An outbreak of rumors claimed strangers planned to kidnap children, slaughter protected deer, or even assassinate a visiting official.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"recur","gloss":"重现","context":"Dry weather may recur, metal fittings may corrode, and a spark can ignite a blaze before visitors notice danger.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"soak","gloss":"浸","context":"They also ask picnickers to soak barbecue ashes, chop firewood only where permitted, and avoid leaving a heap of rubbish that attracts animals to people.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"stroll","gloss":"漫步","context":"Visitors arrive to stroll, admire leaves that glitter without the glare of city lights, and hear insects buzz beneath the trees.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"axe","gloss":"斧子","context":"They inspect a door hinge, replace an axe handle, and check whether emergency routes overlap with crowded walking paths.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"contrive","gloss":"设计","context":"A training exercise asked the team to contrive a response to a sudden fire.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"exempt","gloss":"免除","context":"Nobody was exempt from grief, yet the meeting did not need to become a spectacle.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"hum","gloss":"哼","context":"Children may hum a song or read a trail guide aloud while their parents watch a stream sparkle.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"toil","gloss":"辛苦劳作","context":"Their work remained patient toil: not heroic certainty, but attention renewed each day because the forest could never promise to stay unchanged.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"aloud","gloss":"大声地","context":"Children may hum a song or read a trail guide aloud while their parents watch a stream sparkle.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"chop","gloss":"砍","context":"They also ask picnickers to soak barbecue ashes, chop firewood only where permitted, and avoid leaving a heap of rubbish that attracts animals to people.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"enclose","gloss":"附上","context":"The team would enclose a maintenance record with its annual report, including a note about using harmless dye to trace leaks.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"glitter","gloss":"闪烁","context":"Visitors arrive to stroll, admire leaves that glitter without the glare of city lights, and hear insects buzz beneath the trees.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"ignite","gloss":"点燃","context":"Dry weather may recur, metal fittings may corrode, and a spark can ignite a blaze before visitors notice danger.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"limp","gloss":"跛行","context":"They practiced how to evacuate hikers who could only limp along a steep trail.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"overlap","gloss":"重叠","context":"They inspect a door hinge, replace an axe handle, and check whether emergency routes overlap with crowded walking paths.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"prosecute","gloss":"起诉","context":"Authorities could prosecute real offenses, but fear must not become permission to misunderstand and condemn everyone unfamiliar.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"scare","gloss":"惊吓","context":"A water splash can surprise a nesting bird, and a noisy group may scare a young animal into the road.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"glare","gloss":"刺眼眩光","context":"Visitors arrive to stroll, admire leaves that glitter without the glare of city lights, and hear insects buzz beneath the trees.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"preside","gloss":"主持","context":"One ranger would scout the area, another relay information, and a third preside over the evacuation desk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"roar","gloss":"轰鸣","context":"Outside, wind made the gate slam, and the distant waterfall continued to roar.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"snatch","gloss":"抓走","context":"Rangers explain why nobody should snatch eggs or disturb creatures waiting to hatch.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"undo","gloss":"消除","context":"Rangers tried to undo needless anxiety without dismissing genuine concern.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"blaze","gloss":"火焰","context":"Dry weather may recur, metal fittings may corrode, and a spark can ignite a blaze before visitors notice danger.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"hatch","gloss":"孵化","context":"Rangers explain why nobody should snatch eggs or disturb creatures waiting to hatch.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"heap","gloss":"堆","context":"They also ask picnickers to soak barbecue ashes, chop firewood only where permitted, and avoid leaving a heap of rubbish that attracts animals to people.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"relay","gloss":"传递","context":"One ranger would scout the area, another relay information, and a third preside over the evacuation desk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"splash","gloss":"泼水","context":"A water splash can surprise a nesting bird, and a noisy group may scare a young animal into the road.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"evacuate","gloss":"疏散","context":"They practiced how to evacuate hikers who could only limp along a steep trail.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"glide","gloss":"滑翔","context":"An aircraft would glide above the valley, while crews could irrigate a narrow strip to slow the flames.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"irrigate","gloss":"灌湿","context":"An aircraft would glide above the valley, while crews could irrigate a narrow strip to slow the flames.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"kidnap","gloss":"绑架","context":"An outbreak of rumors claimed strangers planned to kidnap children, slaughter protected deer, or even assassinate a visiting official.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"misunderstand","gloss":"误解","context":"Authorities could prosecute real offenses, but fear must not become permission to misunderstand and condemn everyone unfamiliar.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"buzz","gloss":"嗡嗡声","context":"Visitors arrive to stroll, admire leaves that glitter without the glare of city lights, and hear insects buzz beneath the trees.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"dye","gloss":"染料","context":"The team would enclose a maintenance record with its annual report, including a note about using harmless dye to trace leaks.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"hinge","gloss":"铰链","context":"They inspect a door hinge, replace an axe handle, and check whether emergency routes overlap with crowded walking paths.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"subtract","gloss":"减去","context":"To estimate available time, planners had to subtract delays caused by congestion.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"beware","gloss":"小心","context":"A sign saying 'beware of fire' is not enough.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"blush","gloss":"脸红","context":"A child offered her grandmother a kiss; another began to blush when praised for reporting smoke promptly.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"slam","gloss":"砰然关闭","context":"Outside, wind made the gate slam, and the distant waterfall continued to roar.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"sparkle","gloss":"闪耀","context":"Children may hum a song or read a trail guide aloud while their parents watch a stream sparkle.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"invert","gloss":"颠倒","context":"They could not simply invert the usual arrival route and assume people would leave equally quickly.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"mourn","gloss":"哀悼","context":"After a difficult season, the staff gathered to mourn an old colleague and thank the volunteers.","contextParagraph":4,"collocation":null},{"word":"scout","gloss":"侦察","context":"One ranger would scout the area, another relay information, and a third preside over the evacuation desk.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"slaughter","gloss":"屠杀","context":"An outbreak of rumors claimed strangers planned to kidnap children, slaughter protected deer, or even assassinate a visiting official.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"stab","gloss":"刺","context":"A person who carried a harmless tool should not be accused of intending to stab someone.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"assassinate","gloss":"暗杀","context":"An outbreak of rumors claimed strangers planned to kidnap children, slaughter protected deer, or even assassinate a visiting official.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"corrode","gloss":"腐蚀","context":"Dry weather may recur, metal fittings may corrode, and a spark can ignite a blaze before visitors notice danger.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"A forest station looks peaceful on a summer morning, but its staff know how quickly conditions can change. Dry weather may recur, metal fittings may corrode, and a spark can ignite a blaze before visitors notice danger. Rangers must incur maintenance costs rather than postpone every repair. They inspect a door hinge, replace an axe handle, and check whether emergency routes overlap with crowded walking paths. A sign saying 'beware of fire' is not enough. Safety depends on ordinary preparations whose importance becomes visible only when the familiar landscape suddenly behaves in an unfamiliar way.","zh":"林间站点在夏日清晨显得平静，工作人员却知道情况变化很快。干旱会再现，金属配件会腐蚀，一颗火星就可能在人察觉前点起大火。护林员必须承担维修成本，不能一再推迟修理。他们检查门铰链、更换斧柄，确认应急路线是否与拥挤步道重叠。‘谨防火灾’的标牌并不够。安全依赖日常准备，其重要性只有熟悉景观突然出现陌生行为时才显现。"},{"en":"Visitors arrive to stroll, admire leaves that glitter without the glare of city lights, and hear insects buzz beneath the trees. Children may hum a song or read a trail guide aloud while their parents watch a stream sparkle. Staff encourage enjoyment without allowing play to harm wildlife. A water splash can surprise a nesting bird, and a noisy group may scare a young animal into the road. Rangers explain why nobody should snatch eggs or disturb creatures waiting to hatch. They also ask picnickers to soak barbecue ashes, chop firewood only where permitted, and avoid leaving a heap of rubbish that attracts animals to people.","zh":"游客来散步、欣赏没有城市灯光刺眼眩光的闪亮树叶、听林下昆虫嗡鸣。孩子哼歌或大声读步道指南，父母看溪水闪烁。工作人员鼓励享受自然，同时不让游玩伤害野生动物。泼水可能惊动筑巢鸟，喧闹人群可能把幼兽吓到公路。护林员解释为何不能抓走鸟蛋、惊扰等待孵化的生命，也请野餐者浸湿烧烤灰烬、只在许可处劈柴，不留下吸引动物靠近人的垃圾堆。"},{"en":"A training exercise asked the team to contrive a response to a sudden fire. One ranger would scout the area, another relay information, and a third preside over the evacuation desk. They practiced how to evacuate hikers who could only limp along a steep trail. An aircraft would glide above the valley, while crews could irrigate a narrow strip to slow the flames. To estimate available time, planners had to subtract delays caused by congestion. They could not simply invert the usual arrival route and assume people would leave equally quickly. Panic changes movement, so emergency planning must consider human behavior as well as distance.","zh":"训练要求团队设计应对突发火灾的方案。一人侦察，一人传递信息，一人主持疏散服务台。他们练习转移只能跛行走过陡坡的游客。飞机将在谷地上空滑行，地面队可灌湿窄带减缓火势。估计可用时间时，规划者必须扣除拥堵延误，不能简单把正常进场路线反过来，就假设撤离同样快速。惊慌会改变行动，所以应急规划除距离外还必须考虑人的行为。"},{"en":"Not every alarming story concerned fire. An outbreak of rumors claimed strangers planned to kidnap children, slaughter protected deer, or even assassinate a visiting official. The station refused to spread allegations without evidence. A person who carried a harmless tool should not be accused of intending to stab someone. Authorities could prosecute real offenses, but fear must not become permission to misunderstand and condemn everyone unfamiliar. Rangers tried to undo needless anxiety without dismissing genuine concern. Their duty was to protect the forest and its visitors, which included protecting the public conversation from claims that sounded dramatic but remained unverified.","zh":"并非所有警报故事都关于火灾。突然流行的谣言称陌生人计划绑架儿童、屠杀保护鹿群，甚至暗杀来访官员。站点拒绝传播无证据指控。带着无害工具的人不应被指为打算刺伤谁。当局可以起诉真实违法行为，但恐惧不能成为误解并谴责所有陌生人的许可。护林员既要消除无谓焦虑，也不轻视真实担忧。他们保护森林和游客，也要保护公共讨论不被戏剧性却未核实的说法侵蚀。"},{"en":"After a difficult season, the staff gathered to mourn an old colleague and thank the volunteers. Nobody was exempt from grief, yet the meeting did not need to become a spectacle. A child offered her grandmother a kiss; another began to blush when praised for reporting smoke promptly. Outside, wind made the gate slam, and the distant waterfall continued to roar. The team would enclose a maintenance record with its annual report, including a note about using harmless dye to trace leaks. Their work remained patient toil: not heroic certainty, but attention renewed each day because the forest could never promise to stay unchanged.","zh":"艰难季节后，工作人员聚在一起悼念老同事、感谢志愿者。没人能免于悲伤，但会议无需变成表演。孩子亲吻祖母，另一个因及时报告烟雾受到表扬而脸红。外面风把门吹得砰然关上，远方瀑布依旧轰鸣。团队会随年报附上维修记录，包括用无害染料追查漏水的说明。他们的工作仍是耐心劳作，不是英雄式的确定，而是每日重新投入注意，因为森林从不承诺永远不变。"}],"previous":30,"next":32});
